# Workspace Recipe LLM Guide

## Purpose

Inspect, validate, preview, render, and bench recipes.

## When To Run

- Before creating shaped files.
- When validating recipe drift.
- Between rules and health.

## How To Read The Result

- Listing shows recipes; summary shows inputs.
- Check validates metadata and rendering.
- Dry run shows create/skip.
- Bench writes warp HTML.
- Recipes may compose fragments.

## Examples

- First run: `--list`, `<name> --show`, then `<name> <path> --shell`.
- Keep ownership in `workspace.recipe.roles_map`.
- Bench with a caller-provided `--html reports/<name>.html` or `/tmp/<name>.html`.
- Never pass `--help`, `--docs`, or `--llm` as `--html`.
- Provide required inputs as variables.
- Fix skipped dry runs or failed checks before generation.

## Agent Tips

- Prefer local recipes over inventing scaffolding.
- Inspect a recipe before rendering it.
- Use `--shell` as the convention oracle.
- Run `--check` or dry run before writing.
